cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Predicting 30-Day Hospital Readmission in Diabetic Inpatients with
  Deep Neural Networks
message: If you use this work, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - name: baranlanka
    email: dilidonka@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end deep-learning study on the UCI Diabetes 130-US-Hospitals
  benchmark (101,766 encounters). A Dense DNN, a 1D-CNN, and a diagnosis-
  embedding variant are built, tuned, ensembled, and interpreted under a
  patient-grouped evaluation protocol, with a logistic-regression control.
  The best model reaches ROC-AUC 0.665. The study emphasises honest
  evaluation over headline scores, showing the published 0.48-0.974 AUROC
  spread on this dataset is largely a methodological artefact.
keywords:
  - deep-learning
  - convolutional-neural-network
  - healthcare
  - hospital-readmission
  - class-imbalance
  - reproducibility
  - tabular-data
